# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Extend the existing Part 1 customer storefront into a complete full-stack e-commerce platform.

Build a private owner dashboard that allows the store owner to manage every aspect of the business from one place.

The owner must be able to:

1. Upload and manage products.
2. Upload multiple artwork images.
3. Manage product categories.
4. Update product prices.
5. Manage stock and inventory.
6. Receive and process customer orders.
7. Update delivery statuses.
8. View and manage customers.
9. Manage custom artwork commissions.
10. Track revenue and sales.
11. Manage coupons and discounts.
12. Edit storefront content.
13. Manage shipping and store policies.
14. Manage newsletter subscribers.
15. View sales and business analytics.
16. Configure payment and delivery settings.
17. Receive notifications about important store activities.

All management operations must connect to Supabase.

This must be a real functional management system, not a static dashboard with sample numbers.

# 2. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT RULES

## 2.1 Continue Part 1

Before starting:

- Inspect the existing Part 1 source code.
- Identify the current framework and component structure.
- Inspect existing routes.
- Reuse the existing color palette, typography, logo and design tokens.
- Preserve all existing customer-facing pages.
- Integrate Supabase into the existing application.
- Avoid rebuilding the storefront from scratch.

The Part 1 storefront and Part 2 dashboard must operate as one application.

## 2.2 Admin Access

This is a single-owner platform.

There must be:

- One authorized store owner.
- No public admin registration.
- No customer access to admin routes.
- No customer ability to promote themselves to admin.
- No hardcoded frontend admin credentials.
- No reliance on editable user metadata for admin privileges.

Admin access must be controlled through a database-backed owner authorization record and verified through Supabase authentication and Row Level Security.

Suggested routes:

- `/admin/login`
- `/admin`
- `/admin/products`
- `/admin/products/new`
- `/admin/products/[id]/edit`
- `/admin/categories`
- `/admin/inventory`
- `/admin/orders`
- `/admin/orders/[id]`
- `/admin/customers`
- `/admin/customers/[id]`
- `/admin/commissions`
- `/admin/analytics`
- `/admin/discounts`
- `/admin/content`
- `/admin/newsletter`
- `/admin/settings`

Unauthenticated users must be redirected to `/admin/login`.

Authenticated customers without owner authorization must receive an access-denied response and must never see admin data.

